Aerie-Purpose: Stop a noopener window from a Workspace tab from landing in the default partition.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc (CreateNewWindow)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Prototype for issue 72, option 2. Upstream sends a non-guest noopener window to SiteInstance::Create(), which is the default partition, so target=_blank with rel=noopener would open a Workspace link with the other Workspace's logins. Brave solves the same hole with ContentBrowserClient::ShouldInheritStoragePartition. This prototype needs no new embedder hook. Risk: the prerender branch just below DCHECKs equal partitions, so new-tab prerender must be off for Workspace tabs.

--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
@@ -5825,6 +5825,12 @@
       // as long as they preserve the guest's StoragePartition.
       site_instance =
           SiteInstance::CreateForGuest(GetBrowserContext(), partition_config);
+    } else if (source_site_instance->IsFixedStoragePartition()) {
+      // Aerie: a noopener window must stay in the opener's fixed
+      // StoragePartition (a Workspace). SiteInstance::Create() would put it in
+      // the default partition, with a different set of logins.
+      site_instance = SiteInstance::CreateForFixedStoragePartition(
+          GetBrowserContext(), GURL(), partition_config);
     } else {
       site_instance = SiteInstance::Create(GetBrowserContext());
     }
